{"title":{"en":"Miscanthus Grass","de":"Chinaschilf"},"summary":{"en":"A clump of giant miscanthus (Miscanthus x giganteus) about 1.6 m tall: a dense crown with a fountain of long, narrow, arching blades that droop at their tips, and four stiff flowering culms rising through the clump and ending in silky plumes.","de":"Ein Horst Riesen-Chinaschilf (Miscanthus x giganteus) von etwa 1,6 m Höhe: eine dichte Basis mit einer Fontäne aus langen, schmalen, bogig überhängenden Blättern und vier steifen Blütenhalmen, die durch den Horst aufsteigen und in seidigen Fahnen enden."},"tags":["grass","perennial","clump","plumes","wind","transpiration"],"provenance":{"author":"Semio staffage vegetation content worker","method":"handcrafted","created":"2026-10-29","references":[{"id":"en-1991-1-4","citation":"EN 1991-1-4:2005 Eurocode 1, Actions on structures, Part 1-4: Wind actions. Air density 1.25 kg/m3, F = 0.5 rho cd A v^2, peak velocity pressure (1 + 7 Iv) q_m."},{"id":"en-1991-1-3","citation":"EN 1991-1-3:2003 Eurocode 1, Actions on structures, Part 1-3: Snow loads. Used for the order of magnitude of snow and ice accretion (about 10 kg/m2 on plan area)."},{"id":"vogel-1989","citation":"Vogel, S. (1989). Drag and reconfiguration of broad leaves in high winds. Journal of Experimental Botany 40(8), 941-948."},{"id":"koerner-1979","citation":"Koerner, C., Scheel, J. A. and Bauer, H. (1979). Maximum leaf diffusive conductance in vascular plants. Photosynthetica 13(1), 45-82."},{"id":"jones-2014","citation":"Jones, H. G. (2014). Plants and Microclimate, 3rd ed., Cambridge University Press. Leaf energy balance, leaf area index, boundary-layer conductance."},{"id":"monteith-unsworth-2013","citation":"Monteith, J. L. and Unsworth, M. H. (2013). Principles of Environmental Physics, 4th ed., Academic Press. Penman-Monteith leaf transpiration."}],"notes":{"en":"Six blade bundles (rising and arching bone each) and four flowering culms (lower, arching tip and plume bone) are authored by hand; each blade bundle is drawn as a fan of four blade pieces whose positions follow the bundle bones. The culms stay standing in winter, but shapes cannot be toggled by a pose, so there is no winter-bare geometry; the fourth pose is wet snow bowing the blades.","de":"Sechs Blattbündel (je ein aufsteigender und ein überhängender Knochen) und vier Blütenhalme (unten, Bogenspitze und Fahne) sind von Hand gezeichnet; jedes Blattbündel ist als Fächer aus vier Blattstücken dargestellt, deren Lage den Bündelknochen folgt. Die Halme bleiben im Winter stehen, aber Formen können durch eine Pose nicht ausgeblendet werden, daher gibt es keine winterkahle Geometrie; die vierte Pose ist Nassschnee, der die Blätter niederdrückt."}},"dimensions":{"heightM":1.77,"widthM":2.2,"depthM":1.8,"massKg":10},"materials":[{"id":"miscanthus-blade","title":{"en":"Miscanthus blades","de":"Chinaschilf-Blätter"},"emissivity":0.97,"solarAbsorptivity":0.5,"source":"literature","reference":"jones-2014"},{"id":"miscanthus-culm-mat","title":{"en":"Culms and crown litter","de":"Halme und Horststreu"},"emissivity":0.93,"solarAbsorptivity":0.6,"densityKgM3":300,"conductivityWmK":0.08,"source":"authored-estimate","reference":"jones-2014"},{"id":"miscanthus-plume","title":{"en":"Silky plumes","de":"Seidige Fahnen"},"emissivity":0.9,"solarAbsorptivity":0.35,"source":"authored-estimate","reference":"jones-2014"},{"id":"miscanthus-culm","title":{"en":"Green miscanthus culm (hollow, solid-section equivalent)","de":"Grüner Chinaschilfhalm (hohl, Vollquerschnitt-Äquivalent)"},"emissivity":0.9,"solarAbsorptivity":0.6,"densityKgM3":350,"conductivityWmK":0.1,"elasticModulusPa":2000000000.0,"strengthPa":25000000.0,"source":"authored-estimate"}],"poses":[{"id":"calm","title":{"en":"Calm late-summer day","de":"Windstiller Spätsommertag"},"description":{"en":"Light air of 1.5 m/s: blades fountain freely and the plumes stand upright; drag is a few hundredths of a newton per bundle.","de":"Leiser Zug von 1,5 m/s: Die Blä